{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Behold, I have received to bless.</b> I received a blessing from the Holy One, blessed be He, to bless Israel." "<b>And bless, and I shall not reverse it</b> — meaning: and I shall bless them and not reverse the blessing from them. And it is just that He bless them, for He has not beheld iniquity in Jacob, and therefore ותרועת מלך בו is an expression of endearment and friendship, and this is a great thing, for חזק He is who brought them out of Egypt. אל is an expression of strength [like] ואת אילי הארץ לקח."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:10:02.336238599Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}